  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CareDisc 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A cancer research team is creating a new survey to better understand
    what matters most to cancer patients in early treatment. As a caregiver for a
    loved one with lung cancer, you begin to spread the word in your community, encouraging
    other families to share their experiences. When someone asks how the survey results
    will be used, you explain, \u201CBy helping connect patients, their families,
    and other caregivers with researchers, their input can actually help shape what
    scientists decide to study in early cancer research.\u201D\n\nIs this true or
    false?"
  explanation: "Caregivers often serve as a bridge between scientists and the patient
    community. Their involvement helps ensure early research reflects real-life needs,
    priorities, and challenges faced by those living with cancer, ensuring that early
    discoveries are guided by real experiences \u2014 not just laboratory data. Their
    voices keep research grounded in the human side of cancer care from the very
    beginning."
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
